  "spec": "Owner, verbatim: \"Add a goal to update the project README - I noticed drift\".\n\nREADME.md is the front page for users and was last reworked when the new engine landed (G1017 era). Release 1 has since changed what users see, and more lands before the release: consolidated multi-lens reviews (G1022), declared engine capabilities replacing engine.min (G1027), owner questions that block a design for an interview (G1026), git-flow release lines (G1025), merge-based syncing with a squash to tests + implementation commits and conventional commits everywhere (G1038), clean syncs keeping reviews and a round-based budget (G1039), findings carried on re-run cards (G1040), and the project intent (purpose, who it serves, what it is not, principles) the owner approved.\n\nDrift the owner saw, verbatim: \"It said it uses GitHub for goal storage\". Root's check (2026-11-02):\n- dev's README.md and plugin manifests already say goals live on Git branches (zzzops/goal/*).\n- The published default branch `main` still carries the pre-reset README (\"Goals live in GitHub Issues ...\", \"stores canonical goals in GitHub Issues\"), because Release 1 has not been merged to main yet; it is replaced when the release lands. Confirm the release flow (G1025 release finish) carries dev's README to main and that nothing on main keeps the old text.\n- The GitHub repository metadata is wrong and outside Git: description \"... manage durable goals in GitHub Issues ...\" and topics include `github-issues` and `project-management` (the approved intent says ZzzOps is not a project-management suite). The PR proposes the new description and topics; applying them (`gh repo edit --description ...` plus `--add-topic` / `--remove-topic`) is an external change the owner approves at approve_merge, done at merge.\n\nScope:\n- Audit every claim in README.md against the shipped behaviour on the integration branch at implementation time, and fix or remove each one that has drifted (for example: \"the goal's design starts at once with a worker\" now may stop for an owner interview; what \"human decisions\" covers; install and version notes now that engine.min is gone; release branching).\n- Make the opening paragraph agree with the approved project intent (settings.intent) without copying it wholesale; keep the README practitioner-first and short.\n- Keep links valid; if a linked doc (docs/EXECUTION.md, docs/SKILLS.md, docs/INITIALIZATION.md) has drifted in a way the README depends on, fix that line too or list it for a follow-up goal.\n- No new marketing claims; nothing about the owner's private dogfood app.\n\nAcceptance:\n- Each changed or removed README claim is listed in the PR body with the code, SPEC section or doc that backs the new wording.\n- Links resolve (existing doc link checks pass).\n- The owner reviews the wording at approve_merge.",
  "state": "open",
  "title": "Bring the project README back in line with the shipped product"
}
